speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I have here a petition in the following terms:
The petition of the three hundred-fifty (350) undersigned residents of the City of Edmonton in the Province of Alberta who now avail themselves of their ancient and undoubted right thus to present a grievance common to your Petitioners in the certain assurance that your honourable House will therefor provide a remedy,
The petition goes on to show:
That there is grave dissatisfaction with the present method of mail delivery from the site box system in the constituency of Edmonton West and more particularly in those areas west of 170th Street;
That those residents of such areas now pay tax levies for postal service at the same level as do other citizens in the said constituency who receive door to door delivery and to that extent your petitioners feel that they are being discriminated against;
Wherefore your petitioners humbly pray that the Government of Canada give immediate consideration the institution of door to door postal delivery in those areas of the constituency of Edmonton West not now served which in all respects meet the normal requirements-
